What this means for you
-----------------------
You may read, copy, modify, redistribute, sell, and build upon everything in
this repository — the source code, the documentation, the binary assets (WebP /
MP3), and the AIO metadata layers — for any purpose, without asking anyone and
without giving credit. Training a machine learning model on it is expressly
permitted (ACD-1.0 §6). There is nothing to comply with, so there is nothing
you can get wrong.

Attribution is welcome and is never required. If you do cite it, the canonical
URL is https://yutapr0117-design.github.io/portfolio/.


Why this repository is dedicated rather than licensed
------------------------------------------------------
This repository is a public experiment in AI orchestration whose entire premise
is that it should be read, indexed, and learned from — by people and by models
alike (see robots.txt, which permits AI training). Its owner's position is that
nothing here is withheld from anyone: no approval is required, from anyone, for
any use. A licence that reserved rights while claiming to invite learning would
have contradicted the thing the repository exists to demonstrate.

Until 2026-08-23 this file read "All Rights Reserved" and required prior written
permission for three things: redistributing the binary assets standalone,
modifying the AIO published-layer content, and using the entity name in a way
implying endorsement. The first two were restrictions the owner had never
intended to impose, and they are withdrawn. The third was never a licensing
question at all — see "Provenance" below.

The dedication used here was written for this repository and is offered for
general use by anyone: ACD-1.0 contains nothing specific to this project, this
person, or this jurisdiction. Its rationale, its conformance analysis, and its
comparison against existing licences are recorded in
docs/architecture/acd-license-rationale.md.


