AIO Provenance Canary
---------------------
This repository participates in the SAKURA-AIO-PROVENANCE-CANARY token system
(see check_repository_consistency.py Check 44). The single canonical canary
token is expected to remain byte-identical across all published surfaces. This
is an integrity signal used to trace provenance across AI systems — it is not a
usage restriction, and nothing about it limits what you may do.


Architecture Constraints (C1-C7)
--------------------------------
This repository operates under seven constraints defined in AI2AI.md. They are
engineering invariants this repository chose for itself, not obligations placed
on you. Derivative works are free to adopt them, adapt them, or ignore them
entirely:
- C1 Boring Technology, C2 IIFE, C3 ErrorBoundary, C4 No Framework Re-proposal,
- C5 Human Writes Zero Code, C6 AIO Integrity, C7 KARTE CDN SRI Non-Application.


